# Cross-chat workboard (HARD)

Cursor chats **do not share context**. Shared truth is disk + `.agent/INFLIGHT.md` + SessionMem — not chat history.

## Checklist A / B addition

After reading `.agent/STATE.md`, also:

```bash
bash scripts/agent-workboard.sh status
```

Read `.agent/INFLIGHT.md` when status shows claims or dirty protected paths.

## When you ship uncommitted Studio / Task Manager work

```bash
bash scripts/agent-workboard.sh claim \
  --id short-kebab \
  --chat "short chat topic" \
  --note "what shipped / still dirty" \
  --files "src/library/aiModelsCatalog.js,src/pages/StudioPage.jsx"
bash scripts/agent-workboard.sh refresh-dirty
```

Prefer a **WIP git commit** when the slice is usable. Release the claim after commit or when the work is abandoned:

```bash
bash scripts/agent-workboard.sh release --id short-kebab
```

Store a SessionMem decision (importance ≥ 8) naming the claim id + files.

## Before destructive git (NO EXCEPTIONS)

Never run these on `src/` without the guard:

- `git checkout HEAD -- …`
- `git restore …`
- `git stash push -u` (or stash that includes Studio paths)
- `git reset --hard` / `git filter-repo` that resets the working tree

Required:

```bash
bash scripts/guard-destructive-git.sh --check
bash scripts/guard-destructive-git.sh --paths <each path you will restore>
```

If it **exits 1**, stop. Do not “save dirty then checkout HEAD” unless the user explicitly OK’d discarding those files in **this** turn. `--allow-with-user-ok` only after that explicit OK.

Root cause reference: Sep 8 2026 moat/history-purge chat wiped naming/Stop/garbed work via `git checkout HEAD --` + stash + sync.

